  "behavior": [
    "Unpause optionally stops a playing/ready device. If paused tick is nonzero, call timeGetTime, reload current previous/paused state, add the modulo DWORD clock difference, clear paused, and finally clear playing.",
    "Resume returns unchanged if already playing or start is zero. Otherwise registry byte13 must be exactly1 and actual readiness must pass before issuing set-time-format and play commands. No retry or Sleep is introduced.",
    "Read paused tick after set-format; use it if nonzero, otherwise read current time. Subtract live previous tick, apply the pinned compiler signed abs/division behavior, and add elapsed minutes/seconds to the current packed start.",
    "The pinned SDK MCI_MAKE_TMSF macro takes WORD minute and BYTE second. Do not normalize seconds, carry them into minutes, clamp time or narrow minute early; high minute bits overlap the second field. Both from/to track bytes come from current start.",
    "After the optional play path, a live nonzero paused tick still adjusts previous and clears paused even when configuration/readiness prevented playback. Preserve live state reads after tick/format/MCI boundaries."
  ],
